The low-level JPA approach uses EntityManager query methods directly:

```java
// EntityManager pagination:
List<Trade> trades = em.createQuery("SELECT t FROM Trade t ORDER BY t.amount DESC", Trade.class)
    .setFirstResult(80)   // OFFSET — skip first 80 rows
    .setMaxResults(20)    // LIMIT — take 20 rows
    .getResultList();
// Generates: SELECT ... FROM trades ORDER BY amount DESC OFFSET 80 LIMIT 20
```

Spring Data JPA provides a higher-level abstraction with `Pageable` and `Page`:

```java
// Repository method accepting Pageable:
public interface TradeRepository extends JpaRepository<Trade, String> {
    Page<Trade> findByStatus(String status, Pageable pageable);
    Slice<Trade> findByAccountId(String accountId, Pageable pageable);
    List<Trade> findBySymbol(String symbol, Sort sort);  // sorting only, no pagination
}

// Controller usage:
@GetMapping("/trades")
public Page<Trade> getTrades(
    @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page,
    @RequestParam(defaultValue = "20") int size,
    @RequestParam(defaultValue = "amount,desc") String[] sort
) {
    Pageable pageable = PageRequest.of(page, size, Sort.by(Sort.Direction.DESC, "amount"));
    return tradeRepo.findByStatus("SETTLED", pageable);
}
```

`Page<T>` contains rich metadata:

```java
Page<Trade> result = tradeRepo.findByStatus("SETTLED", PageRequest.of(2, 20));
result.getContent();       // List<Trade> — the 20 trades for this page
result.getTotalElements(); // 500 — total matching trades across ALL pages
result.getTotalPages();    // 25 — 500 / 20 = 25 pages
result.getNumber();        // 2 — current page number (0-based)
result.getSize();          // 20 — page size
result.isFirst();          // false
result.isLast();           // false
result.hasNext();          // true
result.hasPrevious();      // true
// Fires TWO SQL queries:
// 1. SELECT ... FROM trades WHERE status='SETTLED' ORDER BY amount DESC LIMIT 20 OFFSET 40
// 2. SELECT COUNT(*) FROM trades WHERE status='SETTLED'
```

`Slice<T>` skips the count query — more efficient for infinite scroll where you don't need the total:

```java
Slice<Trade> slice = tradeRepo.findByAccountId("SAV2001", PageRequest.of(0, 20));
slice.getContent();    // List<Trade>
slice.hasNext();       // true/false — fetches N+1 to check if more exist
slice.hasPrevious();   // true/false
// NO getTotalElements() or getTotalPages() — count query NOT executed!
// Fires ONE query: SELECT ... LIMIT 21 (fetches 21, returns 20, uses 21st to set hasNext)
```

Sort composition for multi-field sorting:

```java
Sort sort = Sort.by(Sort.Direction.DESC, "amount")
    .and(Sort.by(Sort.Direction.ASC, "tradeId"));
// ORDER BY amount DESC, trade_id ASC

// Alternatively:
Sort sort = Sort.by(Sort.Order.desc("amount"), Sort.Order.asc("tradeId"));
```

